description:
**Company Description**
 Egis has created a single Aviation business unit, pooling together the complementary expertise and services of the three legacy companies Egis Avia, Egis Aviation UK (formerly known as Helios) and Egis Airport Operation. The Aviation BU is one of the largest dedicated aviation teams on the market, comprising almost 300 consultants, engineers and operational experts based globally. A consolidated offering will enable Egis to better meet long\\-term and increasingly global client needs, as well as deliver greater innovation by pooling talent from a unique portfolio of management consultancy, technical and engineering services and operations expertise.




 In the meantime, the Group has also created on March 1st 2021, the Asia\\-Pacific Business Unit, headquartered in Hong\\-Kong which will drive the growth in the region in close cooperation with the various domains of the expertise of the Group, among which Aviation.




**Job Description**
 The Lead Systems Engineer will:




* Be accountable for on\\-site management of the System Engineering Office and all CNS/ATM systems engineering and safety assessment activities;
* Lead and participate in the Design Reviews and Technical Workshops for the various CNS/ATM implementation and coordinate the resolution of Design/Implementation details/changes; and
* Contribute to the development and improvement of systems engineering life cycle processes and deliverables for the Systems of Interest Implementation, such as the System Integration and Transition Program and the Cutover and Technical Support Program.


**Qualifications**
 Education and Training




* A bachelor’s degree in Engineering Science or above awarded by a tertiary institution in any part of the world or equivalent;
* Knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, Power Point, Project, Outlook);
* Excellent command of written and spoken English.


**Experience**
* At least eight (8\\) years’ of post qualification experience in the field of systems engineering;
* Sound knowledge on CNS/ATM systems engineering and safety assurance standards;


 Personal Qualities




* An ambitious personality, capable of achieving;
* Excellent planning and project management skills;
* Strong influencing and negotiating skills;
* Excellent leadership and management skills \\- able to motivate and enthuse, excellent communication, team worker, consensus builder and effective meeting chair;
* Ability to identify and analyse complex issues and suggest and implement solutions;
* Ability to maintain cooperative and effective working relationship.


**Additional Information**
 Specific Responsibilities




* Lead and participate in the design reviews and technical workshops;
* Co\\-ordinate the resolution of design/implementation details/changes;
* Contribute to the development and improvement of systems engineering\\-life\\-cycle processes and deliverables;
* Present regular reports to management.

**職責描述：** 




 Ø Responsible for the ongoing operation and management of Data Centre, network support for the hosting service;




**任職要求：** 




 Ø At least 9 years of IT working experience;




 Ø At least 4 years of computer networking experience in a supervisory role.




 Ø At least two (2\\) years of IT working experience in data centre operation management. Working experience in site preparation is desirable;




 Ø Valid certification of Cisco Certified Network Professional (CCNP) or Cisco Certified Design Professional (CCDP) or Cisco Certified Internetwork Expert (CCIE) or equivalent Cisco certification; and




 Ø Good communication skills (oral and in writing) in both Chinese and English.
